WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.331
Multimedia can reduce cognitive load when it helps learners understand relationships that words alone would make cumbersome.

2
00:00:07.331 --> 00:00:13.368
Diagrams, narration, visuals, labels, and examples can work together to make a process clearer.

3
00:00:13.368 --> 00:00:15.955
But multimedia is not automatically better.

4
00:00:15.955 --> 00:00:25.442
If images are decorative, animations are unnecessary, or narration competes with dense text, the design can increase load instead of reducing it.

5
00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:31.048
Signaling means highlighting or cueing important information so learners know where to focus.

6
00:00:31.048 --> 00:00:39.673
A signal might be an arrow, a label, a highlight, a step number, a short heading, or a verbal cue.

7
00:00:39.673 --> 00:00:47.866
Signaling helps because learners do not always know which part of a diagram or explanation carries the main idea.

8
00:00:47.866 --> 00:00:50.884
Good signals guide attention without adding clutter.

9
00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.040
Modality choices should be purposeful.

10
00:00:53.040 --> 00:01:00.802
Narration can pair well with visuals when the learner needs to inspect a diagram while hearing an explanation.

11
00:01:00.802 --> 00:01:05.977
Dense on-screen text may be better for reference or precise wording.

12
00:01:05.977 --> 00:01:13.739
The problem appears when the same dense text is read aloud while learners try to read it themselves.

13
00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:20.207
Designers should decide what each mode is doing: explaining, showing, labeling, summarizing, or supporting review.

14
00:01:20.207 --> 00:01:22.795
Accessibility must be considered alongside load.

15
00:01:22.795 --> 00:01:29.694
Captions, readable text, keyboard navigation, meaningful alt text, and clear structure help learners access the material.

16
00:01:29.694 --> 00:01:34.869
Accessibility is not separate from learning quality; it often reduces unnecessary friction.

17
00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:37.888
The principle is to keep multimedia purposeful.

18
00:01:37.888 --> 00:01:45.218
Every visual, narration segment, animation, or label should help learners understand, navigate, remember, or apply the material.
